{#- What stands behind the tests (content file 5.1 "Evidence"): the four proof items, each heading
    carrying one proof name in DNA blue. One source for the home page and About, whose "Evidence and
    links" (5.12) adds two text links under them: evidence(links), links an array of { text, href }.
    Import it with {% from "proof.njk" import evidence %}. -#}
{%- macro evidence(links) -%}
{%- set proofArrow = '<svg aria-hidden="true" width="18" height="12" viewBox="0 0 18 12" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M1 6h15M11 1l5 5-5 5"/></svg>' -%}
<section id="proof" class="section" aria-labelledby="proof-h">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 id="proof-h" class="h2 max-w-[44rem]">What stands behind the tests</h2>
      <ul class="proof mt-10">
        <li>
          <h3 class="h3">Approved by <span class="hl">ICMR</span></h3>
          <p><span class="whitespace-nowrap">LitLife™-SCA</span>, our sickle cell test, is approved by the Indian Council of Medical Research.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3 class="h3">Patented in <span class="hl">India and Japan</span></h3>
          <p>The technology behind our tests holds patents granted in India and Japan, and a patent published internationally.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3 class="h3">Working with <span class="hl">CSIR-CCMB</span></h3>
          <p>An MOU with the CSIR-Centre for Cellular and Molecular Biology, Hyderabad, covers developing and commercialising the sickle cell assay.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3 class="h3">Proven at <span class="hl">15 sites</span></h3>
          <p>Population and newborn screening in nine states and Delhi, and a test built for the National Sickle Cell Anaemia Elimination Mission.</p>
        </li>
      </ul>
      {%- if links and links.length %}
      <p class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap gap-x-8 gap-y-3">
        {%- for link in links %}
        <a class="link" href="{{ link.href }}">{{ link.text }}
          {{ proofArrow | safe }}
        </a>
        {%- endfor %}
      </p>
      {%- endif %}
    </div>
  </section>
{%- endmacro %}
